{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of the lotteries and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. In this decision problem, the favorable outcome is defined as '0 Euros' (i.e., no loss), since both lotteries involve potential losses or nothing. For Lottery A, the probability of the favorable outcome (0 Euros) is 99.9%. For Lottery B, it is 99.8%. Thus, Lottery A has a higher probability (by 0.1 percentage points) of the favorable outcome. The decision reason would therefore prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (probabilities of favorable outcomes and their comparison) can be derived from the problem, so the reason is applicable.",
